================================================================================
PART 2: UNDERSTANDING NAVIGATION AND FOOTER
================================================================================

WHAT IS NAVIGATION?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Navigation helps users move between:

• Pages

• Sections

• Features

• Routes

• Important destinations


A navigation area may contain:

• Brand/App Name

• Navigation Links

• Mobile Menu Button

• User Actions

• Search

• Account Controls


For this Grocery List demo:

Navigation
│
├── Brand
│
├── Home
├── Grocery List
├── About
└── Contact


================================================================================
WHAT IS A FOOTER?
================================================================================

A footer appears near the end of a page/application.

It can contain:

• Brand information

• Secondary navigation

• Product links

• Help links

• Documentation links

• Legal links

• Social/profile links

• Copyright information


For this lesson:

Footer
│
├── Brand
│
├── Product
├── Company
├── Resources
├── Legal
└── Copyright


================================================================================
NAVIGATION VS FOOTER
================================================================================

+-------------------+---------------------------+-----------------------------+
| ASPECT            | NAVIGATION                | FOOTER                      |
+-------------------+---------------------------+-----------------------------+
| Location          | Usually near top          | Usually near bottom         |
| Purpose           | Primary navigation        | Secondary/supporting info   |
| Interaction       | Frequent                  | Usually less frequent       |
| Mobile Behavior   | Often collapses           | Usually stacks              |
| Branding          | Common                    | Common                      |
| Semantic Element  | nav                       | footer                      |
| Links             | Primary destinations      | Supporting destinations     |
+-------------------+---------------------------+-----------------------------+


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A navigation bar does NOT have to be:

• Sticky

• Fixed

• Always visible

• Hamburger-based on mobile


Those are design decisions.

In this lesson we choose a sticky responsive navigation for demonstration.


