================================================================================
COMPLETE Navigation.jsx
================================================================================

import { useState } from 'react'

import './Navigation.css'


const NAV_LINKS = [

  {
    id: 'home',
    label: 'Home',
    href: '#home'
  },

  {
    id: 'grocery-list',
    label: 'Grocery List',
    href: '#grocery-list'
  },

  {
    id: 'about',
    label: 'About',
    href: '#about'
  },

  {
    id: 'contact',
    label: 'Contact',
    href: '#contact'
  }

]


export default function Navigation() {

  // ============================================
  // STATE
  // ============================================

  const [
    isMobileMenuOpen,
    setIsMobileMenuOpen
  ] = useState(false)


  // ============================================
  // HANDLERS
  // ============================================

  const handleMobileMenuToggle = () => {

    setIsMobileMenuOpen(
      previous =>
        !previous
    )
  }


  const handleLinkClick = () => {

    setIsMobileMenuOpen(
      false
    )
  }


  // ============================================
  // RENDER
  // ============================================

  return (
    <nav
      className="navbar"
      aria-label="Primary navigation"
    >

      <div className="navbar-container">


        {/* Brand */}

        <a
          href="#home"
          className="brand-link"
          onClick={handleLinkClick}
        >

          <span
            className="brand-icon"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            G
          </span>

          <span className="brand-text">

            GroceryList

          </span>

        </a>


        {/* Desktop Menu */}

        <ul className="navbar-menu">

          {NAV_LINKS.map(link => (

            <li
              key={link.id}
              className="navbar-item"
            >

              <a
                href={link.href}
                className="navbar-link"
              >

                {link.label}

              </a>

            </li>

          ))}

        </ul>


        {/* Mobile Toggle */}

        <button
          type="button"
          className={
            `mobile-menu-btn ${
              isMobileMenuOpen
                ? 'active'
                : ''
            }`
          }
          onClick={
            handleMobileMenuToggle
          }
          aria-label={
            isMobileMenuOpen
              ? 'Close navigation menu'
              : 'Open navigation menu'
          }
          aria-expanded={
            isMobileMenuOpen
          }
          aria-controls="mobile-navigation"
        >

          <span
            className="hamburger"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >

            <span className="hamburger-line">
            </span>

            <span className="hamburger-line">
            </span>

            <span className="hamburger-line">
            </span>

          </span>

        </button>

      </div>


      {/* Mobile Menu */}

      <div
        id="mobile-navigation"
        className={
          `mobile-menu ${
            isMobileMenuOpen
              ? 'open'
              : ''
          }`
        }
      >

        <ul className="mobile-menu-list">

          {NAV_LINKS.map(link => (

            <li
              key={link.id}
              className="mobile-menu-item"
            >

              <a
                href={link.href}
                className="mobile-menu-link"
                onClick={
                  handleLinkClick
                }
              >

                {link.label}

              </a>

            </li>

          ))}

        </ul>

      </div>

    </nav>
  )
}


================================================================================
NAVIGATION STATE
================================================================================

Only this value needs React state:

isMobileMenuOpen


Possible values:

false

or:

true


false:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mobile menu closed


true:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mobile menu open


================================================================================
MENU TOGGLE
================================================================================

const handleMobileMenuToggle = () => {

  setIsMobileMenuOpen(
    previous =>
      !previous
  )
}


Flow:

Current State
     ↓
previous
     ↓
!previous
     ↓
New State


false
  ↓
true


true
  ↓
false


================================================================================
WHY USE A FUNCTIONAL UPDATE?
================================================================================

The next state depends directly on the previous state.

Therefore:

setIsMobileMenuOpen(
  previous =>
    !previous
)


clearly expresses:

TOGGLE CURRENT VALUE


================================================================================
CLOSING MENU AFTER NAVIGATION
================================================================================

const handleLinkClick = () => {

  setIsMobileMenuOpen(
    false
  )
}


Flow:

Mobile Menu Open
      ↓
User Clicks Link
      ↓
handleLinkClick()
      ↓
false
      ↓
Menu Closes


================================================================================
DYNAMIC LINK RENDERING
================================================================================

Instead of manually writing:

Home

Grocery List

About

Contact


we store them in:

NAV_LINKS


and render:

NAV_LINKS.map(
  link => ...
)


Benefits:

• Less duplicated JSX

• Easy link additions

• Consistent structure

• Centralized navigation configuration


================================================================================
NAVIGATION CODE SUMMARY
================================================================================

+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| CONCEPT                  | PURPOSE                                    |
+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| NAV_LINKS                | Navigation configuration                   |
| isMobileMenuOpen         | Mobile-menu state                          |
| handleMobileMenuToggle   | Opens/closes menu                          |
| handleLinkClick          | Closes menu after link click               |
| map()                    | Generates navigation links                 |
| nav                      | Semantic navigation region                 |
| aria-expanded            | Communicates menu state                    |
| aria-controls            | Associates button with mobile menu         |
+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
IMPORTANT: HASH LINKS VS REACT ROUTING
================================================================================

This lesson uses links such as:

href="#grocery-list"


That means:

Navigate to an element in the CURRENT DOCUMENT with a matching id.


Example:

<section id="grocery-list">

  ...

</section>


If the application later has separate client-side routes, you may use your
chosen routing solution instead.

Do not confuse:

# SECTION NAVIGATION

with:

APPLICATION ROUTING


