  }

}


================================================================================
IMPORTANT MOBILE MENU CORRECTION
================================================================================

Avoid:

{isMobileMenuOpen && (
  <div className="mobile-menu">
    ...
  </div>
)}


combined with CSS that says:

@media (...) {
  .mobile-menu {
    display: block;
  }
}


That works, but only because React removes the element entirely while closed.

A clearer UI-state/CSS architecture for this lesson is:

<div
  className={
    `mobile-menu ${
      isMobileMenuOpen
        ? 'open'
        : ''
    }`
  }
>


Then CSS explicitly controls:

.mobile-menu {
  display: none;
}


.mobile-menu.open {
  display: block;
}


This makes:

STATE
 ↓
CLASS
 ↓
VISIBILITY


easy to understand.


